course: dictionary
lesson: 13416
title: Hindrance: the thing in the way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hindrance is something that gets in your way and makes a job harder or slower. It can be a thing, like a heavy bag, or a person who keeps getting in the way. Hindrance is a noun, so you can say a hindrance or hindrances.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The heavy backpack was a hindrance on the steep hill.» A heavy bag makes climbing harder, so a hindrance slows you down. Check by swapping in your meaning: "The heavy backpack slowed me down on the steep hill" still makes sense.
explain: Hindrance can also mean the act of getting in the way, and you can use it without "a": «The river ran to the sea without hindrance.» That means nothing was in its way. Phrases like «a hindrance to» and «more of a hindrance than a help» are useful to learn.
fact: A hindrance is something that makes it harder to do something or slows you down.
fact: Hindrance can also mean the act of getting in the way.
fact: «More of a hindrance than a help» means someone or something made things worse, in a gentle, funny way.
fact: «Without hindrance» means with nothing in the way.
fact: «A hindrance to» is often followed by the thing being slowed down, as in «The fog was a hindrance to the ships».
exercise: «My sore leg was a hindrance, so I could not run fast.» What is a hindrance here? | A new pair of running shoes | A kind friend who helps | A fast, sunny race day | *Something that slowed me down
exercise: «The river flowed without hindrance to the sea.» What does without hindrance mean? | Very slowly and quietly | With a lot of rocks and bends | Only at night | *With nothing in the way
exercise: «My little brother wanted to help, but he was more of a hindrance than a help.» What does this tell you about the brother? | *He made things harder | He finished the job first | He was a great cook | He carried all the bags
test: «The fallen tree was a hindrance to the bus.» What does this tell you about the tree? | It helped the bus go faster | *It was in the way and slowed the bus | It was a pretty tree with lovely leaves
test: Ben says a hindrance is always a person. Is he right? | Yes, but only animals can be a hindrance | *No, it can be a thing, like a heavy bag | No, a hindrance is always a good thing | Yes, only people can be a hindrance
exam: Which word means something that gets in your way and slows you down? | hammock | happiness | *hindrance | harvest
